/* Cloudflare Workers — static assets only. THERE IS NO WORKER SCRIPT, AND
   THAT IS THE POINT. See docs/deploy-cloudflare.md for the button press.

   ── WHY NO `main` ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Cloudflare bills a request only if it INVOKES a Worker script. Requests
   answered from the asset store are free and unlimited on every plan
   (/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/). A Worker with an
   `assets` block and no `main` has nothing to invoke, so every request the
   game makes — the HTML, all of /_next/static, all ~20 MB of models and
   textures, the 404 page — is a free static asset, forever.

   That matters here more than on most sites: one first load of this game is
   roughly 30-60 requests. Route those through a Worker and the free plan's
   100,000 invocations/day stops being "more traffic than we will ever see"
   and becomes ~1,500-3,000 page loads/day — worse than the Vercel bandwidth
   ceiling this move exists to escape. So:

     - DO NOT add `main`. Next builds to a plain file tree (`output: "export"`
       in next.config.mjs); there is nothing for a Worker to do.
     - DO NOT set `run_worker_first`. It is false by default, which is what we
       want; setting it true invokes the script for EVERY request, and on the
       free plan a request over the limit gets a 429 instead of falling back
       to the asset (Cloudflare's own warning, same doc).
     - DO NOT reach for @cloudflare/next-on-pages or @opennextjs/cloudflare.
       Those adapters exist to run Next's server on Workers; they would turn
       every navigation into a billed invocation to render pages that are
       already static files.

   Anything that would need a server belongs on Vercel, which still builds
   from this same branch (vercel.json is untouched).

   ── EVERYTHING ELSE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Response headers come from public/_headers, which the build copies to
   out/_headers; Workers parses it natively and never serves it. Verified
   against /workers/static-assets/headers/. There is no _redirects file — the
   game is one route.

   Local proof that this config is right: `npm run cf:check` serves out/ with
   these exact rules and drives the game in it (test/lib/cf-assets-server.mjs).
*/
{
  "name": "floored",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  "assets": {
    /* The static export. `npm run build:static` writes it. */
    "directory": "./out",

    /* auto-trailing-slash is the default and the right one for a Next export:
       out/index.html serves at "/", and out/404.html is reachable but not
       linked. The app is a single route, so nothing else depends on it. */
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash",

    /* MATCHES VERCEL. An unknown path today renders app/not-found and returns
       404; "404-page" serves the nearest 404.html at status 404, which is the
       file Next exported from that same component. NOT
       "single-page-application" — that answers every unknown path with
       index.html at 200, which would boot the whole game for a crawler
       hitting /wp-login.php and tell Google the URL is real. */
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"

    /* No "binding": nothing can call env.ASSETS when there is no script.
       No "run_worker_first": see above. Leave both absent. */
  }
}
